<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    WHAT IS TRUE OF THIS MACHINE, and nothing else.

    It exists because two halves of gg need the same local convention and have
    nowhere to put it. Gg.Console does not reference Gg.Runner, Gg.Runner does
    not reference Gg.Client, and Gg.Contracts is the wire contract - the artifact
    a customer audits, and the package good-grief consumes from a release. A
    filesystem path is not part of a wire contract and must not ship in one.

    THE CHARTER, so this does not become a junk drawer: local paths and local
    configuration, readable by a runner and a console alike. No transport, no
    credential, no wire type. It carries no package reference and is not
    published; ProjectReferenceTests holds both.

    A second slice - browsing-work-in-the-console - reaches the same conclusion
    for IntentConfiguration and a reader declaration. That is this project's
    second tenant, and the reason it is a project rather than a duplicated file.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
  </PropertyGroup>

</Project>
